0..78 Comment "//! `unwound` models cleanup after a handler abandons a continuation with open"
79..96 Comment "//! access views."
97..100 Comment "//!"
101..176 Comment "//! It proves that captured cleanup runs from the inner access to the outer"
177..188 Comment "//! access."
189..249 Comment "//! It shows a blame when cleanup calls an owed declaration."
250..253 Comment "//!"
254..317 Comment "//! The examples abandon continuations through an exit handler."
318..387 Comment "//! They observe a cleanup call and a list that survives the cleanup."
388..391 Comment "//!"
392..422 Comment "//! - see: #1334 — `unwound`"
423..496 Comment "//! - cites: [Congard-2025-linear_effects_exceptions_and_resource_safety]"
497..500 Comment "//!"
501..688 Comment "//! [Congard-2025-linear_effects_exceptions_and_resource_safety]: https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.23517 \"Congard, Munch-Maccagnoni and Douence, Linear Effects, Exceptions, and Resource Safety\""
